# Document sync

Any work that changes system behavior, APIs, structure, or team agreements **must update** `document/` in the same turn — do not leave code and docs on different versions.

## Layout

```
document/
├── checklist/              # phase + required checklists by area
│   ├── design/
│   ├── frontend/
│   ├── backend/
│   └── infrastructure/
├── knowledge/              # shared knowledge per project area
├── postman/                # Postman collection for handoff/import
│   ├── postman.json
│   └── env.example
└── test/                   # test notes/results (when present)
```

## When to update what

| Path | When | Content |
|------|------|---------|
| `document/checklist/<area>/` | Start/end a phase, new required work, reorder work | Phase checklist + required checklist (mark `[x]` when done); `<area>` is `design`, `frontend`, `backend`, or `infrastructure` |
| `document/knowledge/` | New patterns, architecture decisions, limits/how-to | Per-area notes — e.g. `design.md`, `frontend.md`, `backend.md`, `infrastructure.md` |
| `document/postman/` | API added/changed/removed | `postman.json` (+ `env.example` if new variables) — use skill `/tester` |

## Rules

1. After changing `design/` / `frontend/` / `backend/` / `infrastructure/` → update `document/checklist/<area>/` and/or `knowledge/<area>.md` immediately when needed
2. After changing APIs in `backend/` → update `document/postman/postman.json` (via `/tester`)
3. Checklists must include at least: **phase checklist** + **required checklist** (must-do items before the work is done)
4. **Never** put real secrets / passwords / JWTs in `document/`
